  "hypotheses": [
    "A per-device Qman component must reject a vfio-pci device backed only by a noiommu-N node even when the global unsafe switch is enabled.",
    "For an IOMMU-backed VFIO cdev, the component must bind a real IOMMUFD, allocate an IOAS, attach the device, revalidate exact identity and group facts, and retain the live session until explicit cleanup.",
    "Snapshot epoch and topology hash are only caller correlation in this slice; the component must not claim an authoritative product snapshot binding."
  ],
